---
import "../styles/tokens.css";
import "../styles/base.css";

interface Props {
  title: string;
  description: string;
}

const { title, description } = Astro.props;
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{title}</title>
    <meta name="description" content={description} />
    <link rel="canonical" href={new URL(Astro.url.pathname, Astro.site)} />

    <!--
      Icons. The SVG is the real one: it carries its own light and dark
      variants, so the mark is legible against either browser chrome without
      shipping two files.

      The 32px PNG is the fallback for anything that will not take an SVG
      icon, and it is deliberately the light-theme cut -- a fallback cannot
      answer a media query, so it takes the side that renders on the pale tab
      strips that are still the default nearly everywhere.

      The Apple touch icon is opaque, on `ground`: iOS composites a
      transparent icon onto whatever it likes and the mark would come back
      floating on white.
    -->
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon-32.png" sizes="32x32" type="image/png" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" />

    <!--
      The no-flash path, and the reason it is inline and first.

      A theme that repaints after first paint is very visible on a
      warm-near-black page: the reader gets a white flash and then the site.
      So the stored choice is written onto <html> before any stylesheet is
      parsed, which means it cannot be a module, cannot be deferred, and
      cannot live in a component further down the document.

      Absent a stored choice, nothing is written and the CSS falls through to
      prefers-color-scheme. Three states -- explicit dark, explicit light, and
      "follow the system" -- and the absent attribute is the third one rather
      than a fourth value to keep in sync.

      Wrapped in try/catch because localStorage throws outright in some
      privacy modes, and a theme preference is not worth a blank page.
    -->
    <script is:inline>
      (function () {
        try {
          var stored = localStorage.getItem("ripen-theme");
          if (stored === "dark" || stored === "light") {
            document.documentElement.dataset.theme = stored;
          }
        } catch (e) {}
      })();
    </script>

    <!--
      Preloaded because the two faces are the page. The mono is the display
      voice and the serif is every word of prose, so both are needed for the
      first paint that matters; the italic and the 500 weight are not, and are
      left to be fetched normally.
    -->
    <link
      rel="preload"
      href="/fonts/ibm-plex-mono-400-latin.woff2"
      as="font"
      type="font/woff2"
      crossorigin
    />
    <link
      rel="preload"
      href="/fonts/source-serif-4-latin.woff2"
      as="font"
      type="font/woff2"
      crossorigin
    />
  </head>
  <body>
    <slot />
  </body>
</html>
